#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# difference_delta

#% text
# `difference_delta(f, k)` gives the forward difference `f(k + 1) - f(k)`.

#% text
# `difference_delta(f, [k, m])` gives the `m`-th difference, `difference_delta(f, [k, m, h])` the differences with step `h`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Shifted values of `gamma`, `factorial`, `digamma`, `polygamma`, `harmonic_number`, Hurwitz `zeta`, `fibonacci` and `catalan_number` are written with the unshifted ones, so their differences simplify.

#% item
# A term with a constant ratio `r` gives `f (r^h - 1)^m`, also for a symbolic `m`; `factorial_power(k, n)` gives `n factorial_power(k, n - 1)`; the difference of an indefinite `sum(g, k)` is `g`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
difference_delta(i^3, i)
#% output
#= 1 + 3*i + 3*i^2

#% cell
difference_delta((i^2 + i + 1)*2^i, i)
#% output
#= (5 + 5*i + i^2)*2^i

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
difference_delta(digamma(i), i)
#% output
#= i^-1

#% cell
difference_delta(a^i, [i, p])
#% output
#= a^i*(-1 + a)^p

#% cell
difference_delta(factorial_power(i, p), i)
#% output
#= p*factorial_power(i, -1 + p)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `discrete_shift`, `discrete_ratio`, `sum`
